# Bundled portable Node (Windows-only, ~106 MB): handy locally for building /
# previewing without a separate Node install, but NOT committed — contributors
# install Node themselves, and end users just open MapletViewer.html.
tools/

# Scratch datasets (e.g. an .h5ad export) used to build a sample — not committed.
# sample-data/ ships only the derived demo tsv (merfish-hypothalamus.cells.tsv), which
# IS committed — the dataset users download and open.
examples/
*.h5ad

# The built single-file app IS committed twice, on purpose: MapletViewer.html (download
# & double-click) and docs/index.html (served live via GitHub Pages — Settings ▸ Pages ▸
# Deploy from a branch ▸ main /docs). Both are regenerated by `npm run build:web`, so
# neither is git-ignored. (The Vite build output dist-web/ IS ignored — it's the source
# of that copy, not the committed artifact.)
